{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495340-need-some-help-with-a-small-homebrew-project","id":1495340,"title":"Need some help with a small homebrew project.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-20T19:13:22-07:00","id":1495340,"title":"Need some help with a small homebrew project.","content":"I have a idea that' complicated in concept but should be simple on execution.<br /> The Messianic Voices are the precursors of the celestial chorus,they're mostly the same. But the former is way more Christian than the latter. The Celestial Chrorus these days is just about ready to recruit anyone who recognises that there is a big important One behind all reality.<br /> I thought about making a version of the foundations and pillars of the Messianic Voices but making them based with the multi faith approach of the 2022 Chorus.<br /> <br /> I could think of pillars like<br /> <br /> Bathala (agriculture,growth and nurturing)<br /> Trimurti (power,creation,preservation and destruction)<br /> So maybe instead of basing the Pillars on four archangels,we base them in concepts of monotheistic places, can you help?<br /> <br /> P.S: I know a mage in 2022 wouldn't use the pillars or that the pillars are unusable now. But let's ignore that rule,If you please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T00:53:54-07:00","id":1495347,"title":"","content":"I think this is far more complicated in execution that you're imagining it will be precisely because it's conceptually complex and this is Mage.<br /> <br /> The essential problem is that the Pillars are meant to be more constrained towards one specific groups beliefs, while the Traditions are meant to be &quot;big tent&quot; organizations where disparate belief structures can unify under shared-enough ideological positions. Trying to find Pillars that every monotheist mage agrees on just doesn't seem plausible; because it cuts against the Chorus's ideals that you can you can worship the one however you want as long as it harmonizes with you. <br /> <br /> There's more than four monotheistic religions, so picking places is going to leave some of them out. This isn't even a Chorus specific issue, as the Traditions are supposed to be alliances of like-minded mages from differing groups that DAM would eventually dub Fellowships. You can't even represent the modern Order of Hermes with the DAM Hermetic Pillars effectively and they unified a bunch of Fellowships into one large conglomerate Fellowship way before everyone else did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T08:47:20-07:00","id":1495355,"title":"","content":"For instance, both the Old Faith and the Valdaermen are antecedents to the modern Verbena. And the Messianic Voices are not only restricted to Christianity, they're restricted to flavors of Christianity which put great importance on the Archangels. That doesn't even cover most Protestant sects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T11:23:16-07:00","id":1495363,"title":"","content":"They're not compatible with the Catholic or Orthodox churches either. The Messianic Voices aren't really Christian apart from superficial similarity. They're an offshoot of an ancient Egyptian monist- theosophical cult that is theologically incompatible with every form of Christianity I am aware of. <br /> <br /> A set of pillars for the Chorus would likely rely heavily on that common background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T15:57:45-07:00","id":1495382,"title":"","content":"Understood,keeping those limitarions in mind. Maybe I should do pillars based on common concepts to the many monote\u00edsmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T21:44:00-07:00","id":1495403,"title":"","content":"The problem is that there isn't an simple way to do four &quot;common concepts,&quot; between them. &quot;Monotheism&quot; is a descriptive label for a type of religion. While one specific &quot;family&quot; of monotheism makes up the vast majority of modern monotheists (that is Judaism, Christianity, Islam, and their various less known off-shoots), there are monotheistic religions of other lineages with entirely different belief structures.<br /> <br /> There's also a bunch of religions where their status as monotheists is somewhat debated. The main academic concept of monotheism is heavily skewed by Abrahamic traditions, where there is a strong separation being the supreme deity and any subordinate entities. However there are a few religions where the supreme deity is considered such, and is the primary subject of praise/worship, but has other beings that are treated as being in the same &quot;category&quot; as the supreme deity that might be invoked in religious practice. Some people argue this should be seen as polytheist, others henoist, and others as monotheism (esp. pointing out the roles of angels in the Abrahamic traditions, the Holy Trinity in Christianity, and the veneration of prophets/saints).<br /> <br /> The Chorus is designed towards the most inclusive interpretation (something that has kept groups like the Templars from wanting anything to do with the Chorus despite being a Craft of christian mages). This means the Chorus needs to work for not such members of smaller faiths like Bahai that have some overlap with the larger groups of Christianity and Islam, but branches of Hinduism that see themselves as monotheists (individual branches of Hinduism branch wildly from full polytheism to strict monotheists and not even always agreeing with deity is the supreme one). A lot of non-European religions with fairly strong henoistic tendencies are frequently portrayed as far more polytheist than they would consider themselves.<br /> <br /> To the Chorus all of those monotheist branches, and even many henoist branches of world religions should be welcome members because of their universal acknowledgement of one being that is their cultural representation of The One. Trying to find four universal concepts of monotheism is essentially impossible because monotheism (or something the Chorus would recognize as such even if not everyone would) come from too diverse backgrounds for that (which the Chorus would argue is support for their belief in The One: the worship of a supreme deity is fairly common and everything else below that gets garbled by cultural variations).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T02:36:12-07:00","id":1495408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495340-need-some-help-with-a-small-homebrew-project?p=1495363#post1495363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not compatible with the Catholic or Orthodox churches either. The Messianic Voices aren't really Christian apart from superficial similarity. They're an offshoot of an ancient Egyptian monist- theosophical cult that is theologically incompatible with every form of Christianity I am aware of. <br /> <br /> A set of pillars for the Chorus would likely rely heavily on that common background.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually helps <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a>'s cause. Personally, I would recommend just using the Messianic Voices' Foundation and Pillars as is. Archangels are in no way unique to Christianity; they originated in Judaism, and are also part of Islam. And a case can be made that the different factions within the Chorus have variant notions on just what the Archangels <i>are</i>, ranging from those who take them literally to those who think of them as metaphors for different aspects of the One. <br /> <br /> Having the Chorus use Abrahamic lingo as a common parlance wouldn't be too different from how the Traditions as a whole use Hermetic lingo for Arete and the Spheres. And if the Abrahamic lingo is throwing you, go with some existing Chorister terms: \u201cThe One\u201d instead of Yahweh, Jehovah, God, Allah, etc.; \u201cPure Ones\u201d instead of \u201cArchangels\u201d, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T09:18:10-07:00","id":1495435,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused,are you guys saying new pillars would not make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T09:35:09-07:00","id":1495436,"title":"","content":"I don't know if they'd make sense or not. What <i>I'm</i> saying is why reinvent the wheel? The existing Pillars work just fine for the Celestial Chorus; you need only put some thought into how less traditional Choristers would think of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T10:08:03-07:00","id":1495438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495340-need-some-help-with-a-small-homebrew-project?p=1495436#post1495436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if they'd make sense or not. What <i>I'm</i> saying is why reinvent the wheel? The existing Pillars work just fine for the Celestial Chorus; you need only put some thought into how less traditional Choristers would think of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm... Need to give some thought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T14:49:06-07:00","id":1495459,"title":"","content":"Or another option is to give each of the modern Traditions 2-3 sets of Pillars for its members to pick from (though this will probably require finding some of the fan made ones out there to fill out the gaps) and use Foundation as what unifies them (for example the current group casting rules are kinda vague, but you could be much more specific that characters have to share either Foundation or Pillars to group cast, so Choristers all sharing the same Foundation could group cast even with different Pillars as the Tradition teaches them to overcome their differences and unite under The One, but a Chorister and a Templar both using the Archangels Pillars could group cast even if the Templars have a different Foundation based on their shared understanding of magic practice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T04:24:39-07:00","id":1495476,"title":"","content":"You don't necessarily even need full sets of Pillars. Consider the Order of Hermes and the Craftmasons: they have the same Foundation, and three of the same Pillars; the only change is that the Craftmasons replace Primus with Materia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T13:10:30-07:00","id":1495488,"title":"","content":"But going back to your own specific example of the modern Verbena: they're mostly a combination of the Old Faith and the Valdaermen. Trying to do the modern Verbena Tradition with the Old Faith Pillars + 1 for the Valdaerman part of them wouldn't really work. Especially since there isn't some fifth season to add to the equation that works as a coherent thing in combination with three other seasons.<br /> <br /> It just seems way less work to let &quot;modern&quot; Foundations overcome difference in Pillars than to try to shove the diverse groups that make up the Traditions into one Pillar system (even with some optional alternate Pillars). The Pillars in DAM were already a big stretch for many of the Fellowships and how they failed to really represent the cultures they were supposed to as it was. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T13:18:48-07:00","id":1495489,"title":"","content":"I wasn't trying to diss your suggestion; I was just pointing out that there's an alternative. <br /> <br /> Though I will point out that the Old Faith and the Valdaermen have different Foundations; so they're not actually a good example of \u201cOne Foundation and two or three different sets of Pillars\u201d. Again, I have nothing against the \u201ctwo or three different sets of Pillars\u201d idea; it's just that the Foundation and Pillars system implies (but doesn't explicitly state) that each set of Pillars has a unique Foundation associated with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T05:29:32-07:00","id":1495520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495340-need-some-help-with-a-small-homebrew-project?p=1495408#post1495408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That actually helps <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a>'s cause. Personally, I would recommend just using the Messianic Voices' Foundation and Pillars as is. Archangels are in no way unique to Christianity; they originated in Judaism, and are also part of Islam. And a case can be made that the different factions within the Chorus have variant notions on just what the Archangels <i>are</i>, ranging from those who take them literally to those who think of them as metaphors for different aspects of the One.<br /> <br /> Having the Chorus use Abrahamic lingo as a common parlance wouldn't be too different from how the Traditions as a whole use Hermetic lingo for Arete and the Spheres. And if the Abrahamic lingo is throwing you, go with some existing Chorister terms: \u201cThe One\u201d instead of Yahweh, Jehovah, God, Allah, etc.; \u201cPure Ones\u201d instead of \u201cArchangels\u201d, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be my suggestion, yes. It works for a Chorus that is dominated by the ancient Egyptian proto-religion, which is what we usually see depicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T07:01:41-07:00","id":1495524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495340-need-some-help-with-a-small-homebrew-project?p=1495489#post1495489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I will point out that the Old Faith and the Valdaermen have different Foundations; so they're not actually a good example of \u201cOne Foundation and two or three different sets of Pillars\u201d. Again, I have nothing against the \u201ctwo or three different sets of Pillars\u201d idea; it's just that the Foundation and Pillars system implies (but doesn't explicitly state) that each set of Pillars has a unique Foundation associated with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implication is somewhat undercut by the idea that you can learn Pillars from other Fellowships in DAM. A lot of the narrative reasons this is presented as being rare and impractical would be reduced significantly by the founding of the Traditions, followed by a few centuries of increasing unity within the Traditions as diverse but single entities rather than alliances of similar-minded mages.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Also, archangels are something Judaism got from Zoroastrianism. The concept of angels with specific names and ranks within a hierarchy doesn't exist in Jewish writings or traditions until decently into the Babylonian exile period, and significant exposure and cultural exchange with Zoroastrian beliefs.<br /> <br /> The way these things are getting tossed around like, &quot;well they all have something that we call the same name in English, so they all believe in basically the same thing,&quot; is exactly the kind of thinking that got oWW into trouble for being culturally insensitive. While by the time Christianity and Islam had become full religions in their own right, the concept of angelic classification had become part of the shared religious lineage, what exactly an archangel is, what their job is, how many of them are, and what there names are, varied wildly internally and externally between said three religions. <br /> <br /> There isn't an Abrahamic lingo about these topcis. There's an academic lingo about them that stems from theological study of how various concepts arose and spread through these branching religions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T07:47:02-07:00","id":1495526,"title":"","content":"Well, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> points out, neither the Messianic Voices not the Celestial Chorus are actually Christian, <i>or</i> Jewish, Muslim, or any other real-world monotheists; they're pseudo-theosophists. So it doesn't matter that there isn't really \u201cAbrahamic lingo\u201d, because they're not authentic Abrahamic believers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T14:23:25-07:00","id":1495534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1495340-need-some-help-with-a-small-homebrew-project?p=1495526#post1495526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> points out, neither the Messianic Voices not the Celestial Chorus are actually Christian, <i>or</i> Jewish, Muslim, or any other real-world monotheists; they're pseudo-theosophists. So it doesn't matter that there isn't really \u201cAbrahamic lingo\u201d, because they're not authentic Abrahamic believers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that most Messianic Voices in the period where they are relevant ARE authentic abrahamic believers. We know that Magic works differently, but they don't. It will take a long time before they become as open minded as the modern Chorus is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T14:34:24-07:00","id":1495535,"title":"","content":"